WEBVTT


00:00:59.861 --> 00:01:04.861
[Raspy Breathing]


00:01:33.437 --> 00:01:35.226
Dad...


00:01:39.005 --> 00:01:41.461
Maybe it's the wind


00:01:50.205 --> 00:01:51.798
No!


00:01:54.557 --> 00:01:58.300
Stop! Please! Stop!


00:02:03.966 --> 00:02:07.828
You have a week, Evans.
Then we'll burn the house.


00:02:10.239 --> 00:02:12.213
William


00:02:12.239 --> 00:02:14.213
William!


00:02:22.911 --> 00:02:24.799
William!


00:02:31.807 --> 00:02:35.295
God damn it, William!
William!


00:02:36.128 --> 00:02:39.911
God damn it! Put that down!
Put it down!


00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.495
Let it go!


00:02:45.152 --> 00:02:47.258
It's the last feed we've got


00:03:04.993 --> 00:03:07.197
I'll take care of this


00:03:10.721 --> 00:03:12.544
No, you won't


00:03:42.434 --> 00:03:47.225
Herd's over the ridge by now... you go get cleaned up.


00:03:56.931 --> 00:03:59.320
You lied to me, Dan


00:04:01.443 --> 00:04:03.996
You told me we made payments to Hollander.
- We did


00:04:04.036 --> 00:04:11.904
So, how do you think we bought feed, Alice.
Three months water, the medicine for Mark...


00:04:12.612 --> 00:04:15.874
I had a choice between our family and paying them down


00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:18.562
We're supposed to make decisions together


00:04:18.916 --> 00:04:20.956
Would you have made anything different?


00:04:24.228 --> 00:04:30.820
Alice, we can't make it rain together turn the dust into grass


00:04:31.205 --> 00:04:34.783
We can't stop Hollander from selling our land to the railroad either


00:04:37.861 --> 00:04:45.150
It's too bad the doctors at the aid station didn't take much
of my leg. I read that the pension act pays by the pound now


00:04:47.461 --> 00:04:49.850
Stop looking at me like that


00:04:49.893 --> 00:04:52.162
Are you going to tell the Marshal what those men did?


00:04:52.198 --> 00:04:55.046
Marshal ain't doing shit
- William.


00:04:55.079 --> 00:05:00.774
First thing Mark, I'm going to take you boys, we're
going to round up the herd, then I'm going into town


00:05:00.806 --> 00:05:02.213
What are you going to do there?


00:05:02.246 --> 00:05:04.548
I'm going to tell Hollander to make this right


00:05:05.158 --> 00:05:09.086
I'm going to tell him to pay for a new barn.


00:05:09.862 --> 00:05:12.797
Maybe we should just shoot him like Will says.


00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:42.780
Coach is headed for Bigsby, Boss


00:05:43.332 --> 00:05:48.798
Girded with iron, (?) on top, double shotguns and a Gatling


00:06:34.407 --> 00:06:37.854
You should have let me save the feed


00:06:41.966 --> 00:06:43.821
Ar you going to hock that?


00:06:44.303 --> 00:06:46.212
Some day, William,...


00:06:46.799 --> 00:06:49.734
...when you walk in my shoes you might understand.


00:06:49.775 --> 00:06:52.361
I ain't never walking in your shoes.


00:06:52.432 --> 00:06:54.155
Tracks over here.


00:08:05.234 --> 00:08:07.339
Here we go.


00:08:07.378 --> 00:08:09.767
Giddy up!


00:09:15.061 --> 00:09:17.003
Go man the Gatling


00:09:33.046 --> 00:09:35.348
Mark, stay here


00:09:53.719 --> 00:09:55.246
Down!


00:10:15.704 --> 00:10:18.257
I think they will not follow us anymore.
[They're not going to (?) in a (?)]


00:10:29.241 --> 00:10:31.696
Pull up! Pull up!


00:11:24.699 --> 00:11:27.382
Good morning, Pinkerton


00:11:28.379 --> 00:11:32.503
Name's Charlie Prince, I expect you've heard of me.


00:11:34.908 --> 00:11:40.505
Well, I heard about a balled up whore named Charlie Princess.


00:11:41.563 --> 00:11:43.669
Is that you, missy?


00:11:48.156 --> 00:11:50.611
I hate Pinkertons


00:11:50.652 --> 00:11:52.757
Byron McElroy


00:11:52.796 --> 00:11:56.146
When did your hair turn gray, Byron?


00:11:56.797 --> 00:11:59.317
Go to hell, Ben Wade.


00:12:02.493 --> 00:12:06.900
Well, will you look at all this, you all spared no expense this time, Byron


00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:13.010
I've got to say, thought, It's probably cheaper just to let me rob the damn thing


00:12:17.150 --> 00:12:21.460
If you are going to kill me, just as soon get to it


00:12:23.101 --> 00:12:25.403
I ain't going to kill you


00:12:25.438 --> 00:12:27.445
Not like this


00:12:29.086 --> 00:12:31.988
It won't change a thing, if you let me live


00:12:33.598 --> 00:12:36.184
I'll come for you.


00:12:36.766 --> 00:12:39.188
I'd be disappointed if you didn't


00:12:40.543 --> 00:12:42.136
She's lit She's lit!


00:13:29.889 --> 00:13:31.613
Let's go.


00:13:48.418 --> 00:13:50.141
There we go


00:13:55.330 --> 00:14:01.821
I'm going to ask you to put down the money. Step back.
Tell them to step back or this man will die!


00:14:01.858 --> 00:14:04.192
Not a smart move, friend


00:14:12.995 --> 00:14:14.621
Shit


00:14:19.715 --> 00:14:21.690
He's fast


00:14:31.268 --> 00:14:38.076
Well, Tommy. It seems that there was a Pinkerton
inside that coach that wasn't quite dead


00:14:39.844 --> 00:14:46.783
Now, I know what Charlie told you, because
we don't got but a few rules in this outfit


00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:49.886
This is what happens when you put us all at risk


00:14:55.269 --> 00:15:01.728
Mark, look at me, keep looking at me, back up quietly


00:15:04.036 --> 00:15:05.662
William, look at me.


00:15:26.406 --> 00:15:28.446
Good morning.


00:15:30.726 --> 00:15:34.468
Those are my cattle, I want them back.


00:15:36.774 --> 00:15:40.549
Carefully rancher, that's Ben Wades you're talking to


00:15:44.167 --> 00:15:46.501
I need them back.


00:15:46.951 --> 00:15:48.860
They are all that I've got


00:15:50.407 --> 00:15:54.914
I don't need your cattle, but I will be needing them horses


00:15:55.878 --> 00:15:59.840
So you don't go doing nothin'... Foolish


00:16:20.680 --> 00:16:22.536
Take the horse.


00:16:29.992 --> 00:16:33.767
Find them on the road to Bigsby. Boys!


00:16:47.082 --> 00:16:50.049
They're probably just running late, Mr. Butterfield


00:16:50.089 --> 00:16:55.621
Pinkertons don't run late, that's why they're paid $18.00 a day.


00:17:55.501 --> 00:17:57.224
Get me on my feet.


00:17:57.292 --> 00:18:00.838
- I think you're in pretty bad shape, Mr...
- Just get me on my damned feet.


00:18:11.660 --> 00:18:15.174
Mark, Williams, get me some of them boards


00:18:37.486 --> 00:18:39.275
Can I help you?


00:18:40.046 --> 00:18:45.097
I think maybe a coach headed for here got itself held up in a canyon about 10 miles back


00:18:45.135 --> 00:18:46.662
God damn it


00:18:47.086 --> 00:18:49.356
By Mr Ben Wade himself


00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:51.048
How did you know it was Wade?


00:18:51.087 --> 00:18:53.192
It's been him the last 21 times, Marshall


00:18:53.230 --> 00:18:55.652
I saw a Mexican sharpshooter and an Apache


00:18:55.695 --> 00:18:57.125
God Damn it


00:18:57.904 --> 00:19:00.238
- Did you see the hand of God?
- What's that?


00:19:00.303 --> 00:19:03.369
- His pistol
- Why the hell didn't you do something?


00:19:04.176 --> 00:19:09.358
They had a lot of weapons, Mr..
And they were shooting bullets.


00:19:09.392 --> 00:19:11.279
Let's go, we're wasting time


00:19:23.185 --> 00:19:25.486
Where are you from anyway?


00:19:29.424 --> 00:19:34.159
Tom Conrad bought 1000 heads in Mexico,
hired us to drive them in


00:19:35.857 --> 00:19:38.158
Let's go, Come on, boys.


00:19:50.930 --> 00:19:54.192
Hmmm. Something is going on with the railroad man


00:20:43.635 --> 00:20:47.946
Madame, some whisky for my friends.


00:20:50.836 --> 00:20:53.935
Let's go, the bar is closed.


00:21:16.822 --> 00:21:20.237
Here's to the 4 that we lost in battle.


00:21:21.589 --> 00:21:27.634
And here's to the boss who had to say good-bye to
Tommy Darlen today


00:21:28.598 --> 00:21:30.572
And that's too bad.


00:21:30.614 --> 00:21:32.851
Proverbs 13:3


00:21:34.166 --> 00:21:41.106
"He that keepeth his mouth, keepeth his life. He that opens his lips too wide, shall bring about his own destruction"


00:21:41.175 --> 00:21:42.865
Amen


00:21:42.902 --> 00:21:45.749
Tommy was weak Tommy was stupid.


00:21:45.782 --> 00:21:47.691
Tommy is dead


00:21:50.102 --> 00:21:51.924
I'll drink to that


00:21:56.971 --> 00:21:59.240
Sutherland


00:22:00.043 --> 00:22:02.083
Jorgensen.


00:22:05.836 --> 00:22:07.145
Campos.


00:22:10.143 --> 00:22:12.085
Jackson.


00:22:13.439 --> 00:22:15.349
Kinter.


00:22:32.224 --> 00:22:36.152
Marshal is only half stupid, he's going to be back soon


00:22:39.074 --> 00:22:43.351
They're going across the border, I won't be far.


00:22:44.705 --> 00:22:46.909
I'll wait for you.


00:22:46.945 --> 00:22:49.149
Allright Charlie.


00:23:00.610 --> 00:23:04.025
I've seen you someplace before


00:23:05.282 --> 00:23:06.559
Have you?


00:23:10.466 --> 00:23:13.761
You ever worked for a blind irishman in Leadville?


00:23:16.034 --> 00:23:21.631
I was a singer, the best time I ever had in my whole life


00:23:24.707 --> 00:23:26.495
What made you to quit?


00:23:27.843 --> 00:23:32.829
I got to coughing, Doctor said, I should find a dry climate


00:23:37.187 --> 00:23:40.700
You know, I spent more money in that joint that I could tell you


00:23:42.371 --> 00:23:47.358
Do you remember a girl? Her name was Velvet.


00:23:49.380 --> 00:23:52.696
Nobody forgets Velvet


00:23:58.692 --> 00:24:01.409
You look kind of skinny.


00:24:06.212 --> 00:24:08.188
I feel skinny.


00:24:09.253 --> 00:24:10.715
It's allright.


00:24:13.093 --> 00:24:19.323
I don't mind skinny girls, as long as they've got green eyes to make up for it


00:24:21.733 --> 00:24:23.741
Have you got green eyes?


00:24:35.174 --> 00:24:39.102
That's right, they (?) to be green.


00:24:48.422 --> 00:24:52.766
Do you think they lied? Do you think they stole our horses?


00:24:52.839 --> 00:24:56.134
- They dont need our shit horses.
- Watch your mouth.


00:25:08.327 --> 00:25:10.662
I'll take him into town on my own


00:25:10.727 --> 00:25:16.096
You boys go round up the herd. Don't push
them too hard, I can't afford any more dropping


00:25:16.136 --> 00:25:20.064
Mr, we're going to have to lift you up to get you on top of that horse


00:25:20.648 --> 00:25:22.470
Here comes the cavalry.


00:25:26.952 --> 00:25:29.254
Do as I said


00:25:34.760 --> 00:25:36.736
Is he from the coach?


00:25:36.777 --> 00:25:38.665
The only one that made it


00:25:38.697 --> 00:25:41.763
- Mr. McElroy, can you hear me?
- It was Ben Wade


00:25:41.833 --> 00:25:43.589
Can you hear me?


00:25:44.649 --> 00:25:47.038
This man needs attention.


00:25:47.113 --> 00:25:49.534
Did you see which way they rode, Evans?


00:25:50.185 --> 00:25:52.225
It seemed like they were headed to Bigsby


00:26:39.787 --> 00:26:45.418
You know, there is a little town just south of the border


00:26:46.380 --> 00:26:49.063
Pretty little pueblo
(?) Down by the river


00:26:50.732 --> 00:26:54.507
Folks would pay good money to hear a white woman sing


00:26:55.756 --> 00:27:01.572
Yeah, imagine me shinning on down to Mexico with Ben Wade on my arm


00:27:03.532 --> 00:27:10.211
I'm not wanted in Mexico, Jump out that back windows with me now


00:27:14.925 --> 00:27:17.129
You're crazy.


00:27:21.549 --> 00:27:23.404
- Are you the Doctor?
- Yes


00:27:23.469 --> 00:27:26.567
- Coach got held up
- Get him on the table.


00:27:34.510 --> 00:27:36.004
What's his name?


00:27:36.046 --> 00:27:39.908
Byron McElroy, he's a bounty hunter under contract with the Pinkertons


00:27:47.310 --> 00:27:50.213
You've lost a lot of blood, Mr McElroy


00:27:55.759 --> 00:27:58.923
- That bullet is still in there
- Get it out


00:28:08.463 --> 00:28:10.732
Allright.


00:28:10.767 --> 00:28:13.419
What I'm about to do is going to hurt like a son of a bitch


00:28:13.456 --> 00:28:15.561
It ain't the first time I've been shot


00:28:16.112 --> 00:28:18.021
Hold him, please


00:28:20.752 --> 00:28:22.924
Don't touch me.


00:28:59.538 --> 00:29:06.538
- What the fuck kind of Doctor are you anyway?
- It's nice to have a conversation with a patient for a change


00:29:33.178 --> 00:29:36.277
What the hell are they looking for?


00:29:37.115 --> 00:29:38.806
Ben Wade


00:29:38.843 --> 00:29:41.331
He held up the payroll coach


00:29:42.876 --> 00:29:46.105
- I want to talk, Mr. Hollander.
- Ben Wade in Bigsby


00:29:46.140 --> 00:29:48.955
Shit, we're moving up


00:29:49.020 --> 00:29:50.645
Mr. Hollander.


00:29:50.684 --> 00:29:51.928
Tucker, I'm going to the saloon


00:29:52.220 --> 00:29:54.970
You've got no right to do what you've done, you hear me?


00:29:55.772 --> 00:29:56.982
It's my land


00:29:57.020 --> 00:30:01.177
Come next week it's not Evans, you borrowed a good
deal of money, and I got a right to be recompenceted.


00:30:01.212 --> 00:30:04.955
But you dam'nd up the creek. You shut off my water.
How do you expect me to pay off my debt if you...?


00:30:07.101 --> 00:30:14.935
Before water touches your land it resides and flows on mine. And as such, I can do with it as I fucking please. Go home and pack up.


00:30:17.661 --> 00:30:20.694
Here, if you just give me till spring


00:30:23.964 --> 00:30:26.584
I can turn the corner


00:30:28.382 --> 00:30:32.211
Sometimes a man has to big enough to see how small he is


00:30:33.182 --> 00:30:38.484
Railroad is coming Dan, your land is worth more with you off it


00:31:14.304 --> 00:31:16.540
Hollander!


00:31:26.880 --> 00:31:32.150
You look a little bent, rancher. you come to wake some snakes?


00:31:32.832 --> 00:31:35.320
Dan, would you like a drink?


00:31:35.360 --> 00:31:36.342
No thanks.


00:31:36.385 --> 00:31:39.451
You got your horses back, didn't you? And your cattle?


00:31:41.409 --> 00:31:45.981
Yeah, I got my horses back, but you killed two of my herd


00:31:46.016 --> 00:31:48.405
Hell, they died for a good cause.


00:31:51.489 --> 00:31:57.916
You know, them beasts of yours they woulnd't even fetch $100.


00:32:00.034 --> 00:32:04.671
I'll tell you what. That should cover it


00:32:07.810 --> 00:32:10.111
How much do you get for a day's work?


00:32:10.146 --> 00:32:11.640
2 dollars, when I hire out


00:32:12.322 --> 00:32:14.177
There are 2 dollars for a half-day.


00:32:19.266 --> 00:32:21.721
You took up my boys' time too


00:32:26.179 --> 00:32:29.310
You're right, I did


00:32:36.611 --> 00:32:39.960
Anything else you want to get paid for, Dan?


00:32:42.404 --> 00:32:45.088
Give me 5 dollars extra.


00:32:46.692 --> 00:32:48.350
And what's that for?


00:32:48.388 --> 00:32:50.460
For making me nervous


00:32:51.811 --> 00:32:54.397
Hands up, Ben Wade.


00:32:55.876 --> 00:32:58.243
Boss!


00:33:01.156 --> 00:33:05.826
- Give me your hands, Mr. Wade -
Tucker take his gun - Give me that


00:33:07.365 --> 00:33:09.372
Ben Wade


00:33:11.781 --> 00:33:14.169
Captured in Bigsby


00:33:14.789 --> 00:33:17.756
Be careful with that thing, my gun's got a curse on it


00:33:20.997 --> 00:33:22.820
Laugh while you can.


00:33:22.854 --> 00:33:27.393
Crawley, go get the wagon, make sure every weapons we've got is shot ready


00:33:27.429 --> 00:33:29.502
I'll meet you up front of the office.


00:33:29.542 --> 00:33:31.844
- Get him out of here.
- Sure thing


00:33:31.877 --> 00:33:34.812
I think we should shoot him right now


00:33:35.717 --> 00:33:38.106
Put a bullet right in his nogging


00:33:38.182 --> 00:33:42.492
If you do that, everybody in this shit piss of a town will be dead by morning


00:33:48.391 --> 00:33:57.251
22 robberies, over $400,000.00 in losses, more in delays


00:33:57.735 --> 00:34:04.293
The Southern Pacific will have Ben Wade convicted in a Federal court. Hanged


00:34:04.326 --> 00:34:08.189
...in public, made an example.


00:34:08.680 --> 00:34:11.647
And we will pay to make it happen


00:34:11.720 --> 00:34:14.054
You all notice he didn't mention the lives I've taken


00:34:14.119 --> 00:34:15.974
I need three more men.


00:34:16.039 --> 00:34:18.406
- You can have Tucker.
- Good


00:34:18.440 --> 00:34:20.644
I'm coming, you only need one


00:34:20.680 --> 00:34:22.720
You're wounded, Mr. McElroy.


00:34:22.759 --> 00:34:25.759
I rode in here, sure as hell I can ride out


00:34:25.832 --> 00:34:29.182
- He goes, Potter's coming
- What?!


00:34:30.504 --> 00:34:32.392
Doc can't shoot shit


00:34:32.424 --> 00:34:36.767
I was best shot of my regiment. I'll come


00:34:38.601 --> 00:34:40.902
For 200 dollars.


00:34:42.632 --> 00:34:45.153
You fight for the north or the south?


00:34:45.737 --> 00:34:47.198
North.


00:34:47.241 --> 00:34:52.097
We are southern in name, but Chicago owned.
Fine


00:34:52.169 --> 00:34:53.925
200 dollars.


00:34:53.962 --> 00:34:55.456
Let's go


00:35:06.186 --> 00:35:08.869
- Thank you
- Thank me when it's done


00:35:43.852 --> 00:35:46.634
This town is going to burn!


00:35:50.316 --> 00:35:52.487
Let's get him, boys!


00:36:01.612 --> 00:36:03.914
Get in the coach


00:36:15.180 --> 00:36:20.877
God Damn it. Evans, Crawley, Tucker you need to mount up now!


00:36:20.909 --> 00:36:24.292
Head for Evan's ranch, I'll meet you there with the coach


00:36:39.374 --> 00:36:41.675
How long does he have to be here?


00:36:41.709 --> 00:36:46.663
A day or so, make sure his outfit takes the bait


00:37:14.640 --> 00:37:19.309
Hello there Evans, can you give me a hand with this?


00:37:27.312 --> 00:37:31.884
Whatever your wife is cooking in there, smells good, Evans


00:37:47.856 --> 00:37:49.679
Let's go.


00:37:51.986 --> 00:37:53.993
Good driving, Marshal


00:38:06.961 --> 00:38:09.928
Remind me not to play poker in this town


00:38:11.187 --> 00:38:14.448
Well, Marshal, give us a count


00:38:14.482 --> 00:38:17.231
1... 2... 3...


00:38:35.219 --> 00:38:39.594
Gonna check on my family when you come back, right?


00:38:39.636 --> 00:38:41.010
First thing


00:39:05.245 --> 00:39:07.346
Madam


00:39:09.244 --> 00:39:12.692
Byron, an unpleasant surprise


00:39:14.044 --> 00:39:16.859
What happens if they catch the wagon?


00:39:16.924 --> 00:39:24.660
Well, you saw where his man was, he's still got to go fetsh the outfit. Marshal's got a fast rig, they should reach the fort before dawn.


00:39:24.702 --> 00:39:28.084
His gang can't do anything in front of the whole sixth cavarly


00:39:42.398 --> 00:39:44.886
Did you have something to do with that?


00:39:46.814 --> 00:39:49.269
I hope you are proud of yourself


00:39:52.254 --> 00:39:54.359
Just doing my job, Doc.


00:39:58.014 --> 00:39:59.640
Thanks, son


00:40:17.504 --> 00:40:19.925
We always wait to say grace


00:40:20.415 --> 00:40:22.684
We don't presume to teach other people manners


00:40:22.719 --> 00:40:25.371
Aren't we supposed to say grace for murderers too?


00:40:25.408 --> 00:40:28.408
- Grace is for everyone, dear
- Then why don't we say it?


00:40:28.448 --> 00:40:31.580
Mark, I'd like to hear it.


00:40:36.576 --> 00:40:40.504
God, our father, Lord and Savior, thank you for your love and favor


00:40:40.576 --> 00:40:45.846
Please bless this drink and food we pray, and bless all who share with us today


00:40:45.888 --> 00:40:47.384
Amen.


00:40:48.481 --> 00:40:50.106
Amen.


00:40:51.169 --> 00:40:56.155
If my Pa' wanted to, he could shoot you dead, he can shoot a jack rabbit at 50 yards


00:40:56.993 --> 00:41:00.954
Shooting an animal is a lot different than shooting a man, son


00:41:01.025 --> 00:41:06.044
Not, it isn't not in my opinion.


00:41:07.457 --> 00:41:15.325
We can ask Byron here, now Byron he's killed dozens
of people, men, women and children. Miners, Apaches


00:41:16.002 --> 00:41:20.159
Not a soul I've taken, that didn't deserve what they've got


00:41:21.186 --> 00:41:28.736
"Every way of a man is right in his own eyes", Byron,
"but the Lord ponders the heart"


00:41:30.531 --> 00:41:32.920
Proverbs 21


00:41:47.043 --> 00:41:48.799
Dan


00:41:53.956 --> 00:41:57.022
You eat more when you're nervous, Mr Butterfield?


00:41:57.988 --> 00:42:02.593
Why, thank you Dan, how pleasant and kind of you,
Much appreciated it


00:42:03.076 --> 00:42:08.516
Could you cut that for me? Could you cut that fat out,
I don't particularly like the fat at all.


00:42:09.060 --> 00:42:10.751
Allright.


00:42:13.092 --> 00:42:16.541
And the grissle, I don't like grissle.


00:42:22.949 --> 00:42:25.851
Do you mind if I ask you how you got that hitch in your step, Dan?


00:42:25.893 --> 00:42:28.349
Don't tell him nothing, Mr Evans.


00:42:31.653 --> 00:42:34.239
Where were you stationed?


00:42:35.877 --> 00:42:39.806
7th company sharpshooters, out of Leadville Mass.


00:42:43.910 --> 00:42:48.034
My father was defending the US capital in the D.C.


00:42:48.998 --> 00:42:52.576
Isn't that so? Well Dan, Tell me the story of how you lost your leg


00:42:53.318 --> 00:42:58.206
Did they shoot it off? Cut it off? Did the Indians do it?


00:43:08.487 --> 00:43:11.073
I saw something over there in the grass.


00:43:19.143 --> 00:43:21.183
There ain't nothing


00:43:29.514 --> 00:43:34.514
What if they caught up with the coach already?
What if they already know it's Crawley inside?


00:43:37.256 --> 00:43:39.623
Have you ever been to San Francisco?


00:43:41.736 --> 00:43:45.414
If it's all right by you Mr. Wade, I rather we not talk


00:43:46.281 --> 00:43:48.736
So you've never been in San Francisco?


00:43:49.993 --> 00:43:51.040
No.


00:43:55.017 --> 00:43:58.978
I know a girl there, she's the daughter of a sea captain


00:43:59.017 --> 00:44:01.887
She had the most beautiful green eyes


00:44:03.145 --> 00:44:05.863
The greenest eyes I ever saw


00:44:11.242 --> 00:44:13.347
Like yours.


00:44:17.002 --> 00:44:20.712
When I stared deep into them they'd
just change color in front of me


00:44:20.746 --> 00:44:23.168
All the colors of the sea.


00:44:31.595 --> 00:44:33.799
What did you say your name was again?


00:44:34.379 --> 00:44:36.037
Alice.


00:44:48.299 --> 00:44:52.009
For God's sake, he's killed more men than the drought.


00:44:52.044 --> 00:44:53.767
He is not what I expected


00:44:54.156 --> 00:44:57.451
He is dangerous, "Dangerous" is what he is, Alice.


00:44:57.932 --> 00:45:00.583
I don't want you or the boys talking to him


00:45:02.156 --> 00:45:07.241
You can change your mind Dan, none will think less of you


00:45:08.556 --> 00:45:12.003
None can think less of me


00:45:13.197 --> 00:45:16.710
6 months from now, everything is going to be great


00:45:17.261 --> 00:45:19.235
Cows are going to be fat


00:45:19.661 --> 00:45:22.890
We might even see the steam from the train coming over the ridge


00:45:24.173 --> 00:45:31.723
We will be allright, but we won't make it
through the next 6 days, if I don't do this


00:45:36.750 --> 00:45:40.098
Sorry, Dan. McElroy says 5 minutes


00:45:51.054 --> 00:45:53.901
Do you think it's too much for me?


00:45:55.246 --> 00:45:57.450
He's a killer, Daniel.


00:45:58.222 --> 00:46:03.307
Yet somehow I have the decency to bring him to justice.


00:46:07.343 --> 00:46:10.060
What are you thinking?


00:46:11.087 --> 00:46:15.243
I am not out there alone, have a little faith in me!


00:46:16.110 --> 00:46:20.203
Ben Wade has a gang, and they're out there tonight, somewhere


00:46:20.240 --> 00:46:26.023
If I don't go, we have to pack up and leave
and God knows where w/o a prayer to (?)


00:46:26.096 --> 00:46:30.439
Now, I am tired, Alice I'm tired of watching my boys go hungry


00:46:30.511 --> 00:46:34.537
...I'm tired of the way they look at
me, I'm tired of the way that you don't


00:46:35.216 --> 00:46:43.084
I've been standing on one leg for 3 damned
years, waiting for God to do me a favor


00:46:45.393 --> 00:46:47.498
And he ain't listening


00:46:49.137 --> 00:46:50.511
Mr. Evans.


00:47:01.425 --> 00:47:05.649
No, no, no. This is my horse now


00:47:09.009 --> 00:47:10.831
Come over here


00:47:18.257 --> 00:47:21.606
- Don't give me any trouble, Mark
- Yes, sir


00:47:25.010 --> 00:47:26.637
Boy.


00:47:26.707 --> 00:47:28.878
- I want to come with you
- Well, you can't


00:47:28.915 --> 00:47:30.028
I can help.


00:47:30.067 --> 00:47:32.074
You're 14 years old.


00:47:32.115 --> 00:47:35.628
I can ride faster and you shoot better than any one of them.


00:47:35.667 --> 00:47:40.904
The Pinkerton is hurt, Potter is no good, that
railroad man is dead weight, and that other bastard...


00:47:41.683 --> 00:47:44.847
I dont have time to argue I need you here.


00:47:44.883 --> 00:47:46.672
That's that That's that


00:47:52.819 --> 00:47:55.503
So, boys, where are we headed?


00:47:55.540 --> 00:48:04.716
It ain't none of your business where we are headed Wade, you're a prisoner, you don't speak, you don't piss, you don't god damn breathe unless we say so.


00:48:05.140 --> 00:48:07.311
Do you understand that?


00:48:10.229 --> 00:48:16.274
We're taking you to Contention, putting
you on the 3:10 to Yuma, day after tomorrow


00:48:16.309 --> 00:48:18.131
You shouldn't have told him, now.


00:48:18.581 --> 00:48:23.699
Relax, friend. Now if we get separated,
I'll know where to meet up


00:48:27.157 --> 00:48:32.787
I'd like to thank you for your hospitality Madame,
I hope I can send your husband back allright


00:49:05.238 --> 00:49:09.646
What did Ben Wade mean about sending Pa' back all right?
Is he saying he was going to kill him?


00:49:09.686 --> 00:49:13.996
Ben Wade don't have to lift a finger, his gang will do it for him.


00:49:16.471 --> 00:49:19.374
Your father can take care of himself


00:50:02.650 --> 00:50:08.912
So, were you conscripted into Lincoln's
army, Mr. Evans? Or did you volunteered?


00:50:08.953 --> 00:50:10.961
Neither...


00:50:12.889 --> 00:50:14.264
Maybe both.


00:50:14.297 --> 00:50:16.021
What does that means?


00:50:16.506 --> 00:50:25.912
It means I was a volunteer for the Mass. State Guard, then in 62 the Federal government was running low on men, so they called in the state militias


00:50:26.490 --> 00:50:30.647
- To protect Washinton.
- And that's when you got hurt


00:50:34.458 --> 00:50:39.826
What are you doing out here, Dan?
You've got a family to protect.


00:50:40.890 --> 00:50:44.633
You are not a law man, you don't work for the railroad like Mr. shiney shoes over there


00:50:44.666 --> 00:50:47.034
Not a Pinkerton


00:50:47.803 --> 00:50:52.113
Maybe I don't like the idea of men like you running loose


00:50:52.315 --> 00:50:55.960
It's man's nature to take what he wants, Dan


00:50:55.995 --> 00:50:57.751
It's how we are born


00:50:57.788 --> 00:51:01.650
Well, I make an honest living


00:51:01.724 --> 00:51:05.019
It might be honest, but I don't think it's much of a living


00:51:05.052 --> 00:51:08.086
you must be hurting bad for money, to take this job


00:51:09.725 --> 00:51:11.547
Go to sleep.


00:51:15.708 --> 00:51:18.872
I imagine debt puts a lot of pressure on a marriage


00:51:18.940 --> 00:51:22.585
Are you married? What would you know about marriage?


00:51:23.740 --> 00:51:26.740
We can't all be cut-throats and thieves


00:51:26.812 --> 00:51:31.123
Well, I know that if I was lucky enough to have a wife like
Alice, I'd treat her a whole lot better than you do, Dan


00:51:31.838 --> 00:51:37.272
I'd feed her better, I'd buy her pretty dresses.
I wouldn't make her work so hard.


00:51:39.774 --> 00:51:43.287
Yeah, I'd bet Alice was a real pretty girl before she married you...


00:51:43.326 --> 00:51:50.331
Don't talk about my wife, you shut up about her.
You say one more word and I'll cut your tongue out.


00:51:52.927 --> 00:51:55.578
I'd like the sight of it if you did.


00:51:55.614 --> 00:51:57.338
Mr. Evans.


00:52:03.902 --> 00:52:06.488
It's my watch, now


00:52:51.348 --> 00:52:54.590
I suppose it's too much to ask for a little quiet.


00:52:55.744 --> 00:53:01.659
The way I figured it: I'd be asleep in my own bed right now, if it weren't for you


00:53:02.305 --> 00:53:06.713
So if I've got to be up, you damn well be up with me too,


00:53:06.753 --> 00:53:09.404
Ben Wade.


00:53:40.418 --> 00:53:42.557
Son of a bitch!


00:53:57.655 --> 00:53:59.510
Enough.


00:54:02.935 --> 00:54:05.903
- Enough!
- That's enough, McElroy


00:54:18.233 --> 00:54:20.338
We have to bury him.


00:54:21.176 --> 00:54:26.773
If you take the time to dig one grave
you might as well dig one for yourself


00:54:29.721 --> 00:54:32.379
Let's go. Mount up


00:55:57.266 --> 00:56:00.811
Don't worry there, Boss We're going
to get you out of there in a second


00:56:15.237 --> 00:56:17.474
Wait! Wait!


00:56:18.887 --> 00:56:21.276
Sutherland.


00:56:25.318 --> 00:56:27.041
Jackson


00:56:35.719 --> 00:56:36.929
No, No. Don't do this


00:56:37.702 --> 00:56:41.631
Don't do this. Don't do this.


00:56:41.898 --> 00:56:42.847
Where is he?


00:56:43.179 --> 00:56:45.928
Open the door. Open the door!
Let me out of here, God damn it!


00:56:46.219 --> 00:56:47.080
Where did they take him?


00:56:47.467 --> 00:56:48.514
I don't know!


00:56:53.643 --> 00:56:56.610
Mr... you'd better tell
me where they took him...


00:56:57.931 --> 00:56:59.305
...or you will burn


00:57:05.803 --> 00:57:06.665
Contention! Allright?!


00:57:07.436 --> 00:57:08.680
They're going to Contention


00:57:09.260 --> 00:57:12.708
They're going to put him on the 3:10 to Yuma prison train. Tomorrow


00:57:16.748 --> 00:57:17.795
Let me go out of here!


00:57:21.259 --> 00:57:25.963
Contention is... 80 miles back the other way.


00:57:26.829 --> 00:57:28.170
They've just about killed our horses


00:57:28.557 --> 00:57:30.084
So, we'll buy new ones.


00:57:31.724 --> 00:57:34.626
Charlie, it's his own fault he got caught, he made a mistake.


00:57:37.389 --> 00:57:39.658
You think you can do a better job leading this group?


00:57:40.397 --> 00:57:41.160
Maybe...


00:57:46.861 --> 00:57:49.993
You've forgotten what he done for us?


00:57:56.333 --> 00:57:57.479
We're going to Contention!


00:58:09.391 --> 00:58:11.398
Can't say I didn't warn you


00:58:14.895 --> 00:58:16.324
There's a shortcut we can take


00:58:17.359 --> 00:58:18.024
A shortcut?


00:58:18.735 --> 00:58:19.683
Through the pass


00:58:20.239 --> 00:58:21.482
It takes you right through Contention


00:58:21.871 --> 00:58:22.853
Why didnt you say something before?


00:58:23.310 --> 00:58:24.739
It's Apache country


00:58:25.422 --> 00:58:28.902
- I thought that the government gave them land.
- These are the ones who refused to go.


00:58:29.359 --> 00:58:31.662
- I wouldn't take that path
- You want us to take the long way?


00:58:31.984 --> 00:58:33.991
- That's right
- and let your boys catch us?


00:58:36.399 --> 00:58:40.556
Mr.. Butterfield, the Apache who lived in
that path are the ones that stayed to fight


00:58:41.680 --> 00:58:43.022
They enjoy killing


00:58:44.175 --> 00:58:45.223
You ain't going to make it


00:58:48.975 --> 00:58:50.601
We'll take our chances


00:59:18.098 --> 00:59:19.504
Something on your mind, Dan?


00:59:21.554 --> 00:59:22.601
Why did you kill Tucker?


00:59:23.953 --> 00:59:26.157
Why not me? Or Butterfield?


00:59:27.025 --> 00:59:28.519
Hell, Tucker took my horse.


00:59:30.578 --> 00:59:32.585
Did you liked him, Dan?
- No


00:59:34.449 --> 00:59:36.337
He told me he burned down your barn


00:59:38.450 --> 00:59:39.399
He was an asshole


00:59:41.363 --> 00:59:43.730
But wishing him dead and killing him are two different things


00:59:44.787 --> 00:59:46.609
Your conscience is sensitive, Dan


00:59:47.379 --> 00:59:48.939
I don't think it's my favorite part of you.


00:59:50.195 --> 00:59:54.766
(?), Mr. Wade. If you want to talk to somebody, talk to me.


00:59:55.859 --> 00:59:57.266
I don't like talking to you, Byron


00:59:57.875 --> 00:59:59.282
Not when I have the gun.


00:59:59.859 --> 01:00:02.675
No, that ain't it, I just don't find you that interesting.


01:00:03.892 --> 01:00:06.281
Laugh it up, Doc. 'till he guts you like a fish


01:00:06.964 --> 01:00:08.490
Byron is like a song with one note


01:00:09.267 --> 01:00:11.504
Did you ever read another book in your life, Byron.
Besides the Bible?


01:00:11.987 --> 01:00:12.848
No need


01:00:16.884 --> 01:00:19.535
Byron acts pius, a few years ago when
he was under contract with Central,


01:00:20.308 --> 01:00:22.545
I've seen him and a
bunch of brother Pink'ts...


01:00:23.285 --> 01:00:25.227
...mow down 32 Apache women and children


01:00:26.356 --> 01:00:29.373
Renegades. Gunning down railroad
men and their families...


01:00:29.717 --> 01:00:31.889
...picking them off the road, one by one. Scalped.


01:00:32.916 --> 01:00:36.211
There was young'nes running around.
Crying and screaming, no more than 3 years old


01:00:36.885 --> 01:00:40.496
...and his boys shot them all and pushed them into a ditch


01:00:40.821 --> 01:00:42.315
Some of them were still crying


01:00:44.822 --> 01:00:48.367
I guess Byron figured that Jesus wouldn't mind


01:00:50.293 --> 01:00:52.333
Apparently Jesus don't like the Apache


01:00:53.845 --> 01:00:54.893
Keep on talking...


01:00:56.117 --> 01:01:02.698
All the way to Yuma. Right up on them steps to the rope. Straight to hell


01:01:03.541 --> 01:01:04.785
Yeah, the day I die, Byron


01:01:05.686 --> 01:01:07.181
I'm getting sprung from hell


01:01:07.894 --> 01:01:14.386
I might feel the same, if I'd come from the seed of
a drunk grave digger and the rancid womb of a whore


01:01:28.054 --> 01:01:28.720
Drop it, Dan Evans. Drop it


01:01:29.496 --> 01:01:30.543
Toss it to the ground, Doc


01:01:31.927 --> 01:01:33.171
Mr. Butterfield...


01:01:36.791 --> 01:01:42.836
I believe Dan, you're carrying a pistol as well.
I'd appreciate it if you take it out and drop it on the ground. Thank you


01:01:49.195 --> 01:01:51.934
Now, I've always liked you, Byron,...


01:01:51.969 --> 01:01:54.673
..., but you never knew when to shut up


01:01:58.776 --> 01:02:00.881
Even bad men love their mommas


01:02:06.104 --> 01:02:07.992
Now I think it's time for everybody to go home


01:02:09.176 --> 01:02:10.386
Don't you move, Mr. Wade.


01:02:11.352 --> 01:02:12.497
Let go of that shotgun.


01:02:14.521 --> 01:02:16.823
William, what the hell are you doing here?


01:02:18.361 --> 01:02:21.783
I don't think that you're going to shoot
a man handcuffed in the back of the head, boy


01:02:22.906 --> 01:02:25.477
Dan, tell your boy it's over


01:02:26.586 --> 01:02:29.041
You think you can keep you gun on him, William?


01:02:30.105 --> 01:02:33.015
I'm doing a damn sight better than you did


01:03:17.360 --> 01:03:19.083
You ever been to Dodge City?


01:03:22.832 --> 01:03:23.780
No.


01:03:25.456 --> 01:03:26.601
Stop talking to him


01:03:31.728 --> 01:03:34.095
The way you're shuffling those cards, I took you for a pro


01:03:35.440 --> 01:03:36.585
I practice a lot.


01:03:37.200 --> 01:03:37.931
I can tell


01:03:45.905 --> 01:03:46.854
You ever been to Dodge?


01:03:47.345 --> 01:03:48.293
Yes, indeed


01:03:49.681 --> 01:03:52.234
Meanest, most beautiful, dirty city there ever was


01:03:52.721 --> 01:03:58.123
Saloons just overflowing with cattle drivers and road
agents, prospectors, gunslingers, gamblers and women


01:04:01.457 --> 01:04:03.312
Women will do things to you, you'll never forget.


01:04:05.682 --> 01:04:07.307
They'll give you disease you'll never forget


01:04:07.730 --> 01:04:10.959
Money in your pocket in Dodge City, you can have everything a man ever wished for


01:04:13.682 --> 01:04:14.926
Everything a man comes to need


01:04:18.674 --> 01:04:20.878
I got (?) I was a boy not much bigger than you


01:04:22.451 --> 01:04:24.752
Now, how many men have you killed since then, Wade?


01:04:27.795 --> 01:04:29.224
How many families have you destroyed?


01:04:33.691 --> 01:04:35.895
Quite a few


01:04:39.260 --> 01:04:44.148
Is it true that you dynamited a wagon full of prospectors
in the Western Territories last spring?


01:04:44.924 --> 01:04:45.785
No, that's a lie.


01:04:46.940 --> 01:04:48.183
It was a train full


01:04:57.244 --> 01:04:58.259
(?), Dan


01:05:01.520 --> 01:05:02.698
I gotta take a piss


01:05:05.745 --> 01:05:07.533
You know, I thought he was going to shoot me back in the ravine


01:05:09.520 --> 01:05:10.764
I really thought he was going to do it


01:05:11.077 --> 01:05:12.637
There was a wildness in his eyes, he reminds me...


01:05:13.061 --> 01:05:14.370
He's going to be nothing like you, Wade


01:05:20.293 --> 01:05:22.749
A man's got to have a head start on the path of decency


01:05:25.477 --> 01:05:28.063
Yeah, that's why I don't mess
around with doing anything good, Dan.


01:05:33.125 --> 01:05:34.588
You do one good deed for somebody...


01:05:36.134 --> 01:05:37.563
I imagine it's habit forming


01:05:39.399 --> 01:05:43.010
Something decent, see that grateful look in their eyes...


01:05:43.622 --> 01:05:45.510
...I imagine it makes you feel like christ hisself


01:05:45.894 --> 01:05:48.196
I've had enough of this Wade, come on.
Let's go


01:06:41.098 --> 01:06:43.203
It's three of them -Yours?


01:06:43.689 --> 01:06:44.933
If they were mine, you'd be dead


01:06:48.297 --> 01:06:49.246
Give me that gun, Wade!


01:07:38.155 --> 01:07:39.235
I told you not to come this way


01:07:40.363 --> 01:07:41.738
It was McElroy's decision.


01:07:42.219 --> 01:07:43.332
I told you there'd be trouble


01:07:48.908 --> 01:07:50.053
Give me the keys to the handcuffs


01:08:16.121 --> 01:08:17.136
Easy. Easy now


01:08:18.489 --> 01:08:19.383
Where is he?


01:08:20.217 --> 01:08:21.013
He's gone


01:08:23.821 --> 01:08:27.025
He took the horses with him, I found this in the grass


01:08:33.506 --> 01:08:38.262
That's the quickest way out of the pass, he'll
be looking for help, to get his cuffs off


01:08:39.958 --> 01:08:41.168
We are going after him.


01:08:42.422 --> 01:08:45.291
There ain't no reward for getting
him halfway to that train, is there?


01:09:56.473 --> 01:09:59.539
I've got to be honest with you, I like some of their food.


01:10:00.122 --> 01:10:02.708
As for wanting $40 a month now, I can...


01:10:04.186 --> 01:10:05.113
Hello, Love.


01:10:06.298 --> 01:10:10.072
God damned Coolies, they'll work just
fine with my left boot up their ass


01:10:10.362 --> 01:10:12.533
Well, if I could teach a monkey to lay track,...


01:10:13.818 --> 01:10:16.404
Well. What we need here are some
negros brought here, Mister Boles


01:10:16.890 --> 01:10:18.581
Show these Chinamen what real work is


01:10:26.939 --> 01:10:28.368
Holly Christ!


01:10:30.011 --> 01:10:31.058
Who is that?


01:10:32.027 --> 01:10:33.074
That's him!


01:10:35.963 --> 01:10:38.101
Help me with the handcuffs


01:10:40.954 --> 01:10:42.710
Break the chain. Use the hammer, break the chain.


01:10:46.908 --> 01:10:49.625
I have 5 guns on you out here, Ben Wade


01:10:50.172 --> 01:10:51.219
Just come on out!


01:11:10.077 --> 01:11:10.873
The horses.


01:11:33.118 --> 01:11:34.165
What the hell is going on here?


01:11:37.342 --> 01:11:40.212
Mr. Butterfield, all finished in Bigsby?


01:11:40.702 --> 01:11:41.465
Mr. Boles


01:11:49.470 --> 01:11:52.635
You'd better hurry, we're making the last
blasts through the mountains this week.


01:11:53.214 --> 01:11:54.043
That's my prisoner.


01:11:54.559 --> 01:11:57.242
We're taking him to Contention,
putting him on the prison train to Yuma.


01:11:58.655 --> 01:11:59.800
What prisoner?


01:12:00.767 --> 01:12:03.963
Come now, Mr. Boles, that's Ben Wade you have there


01:12:04.638 --> 01:12:08.217
Ben Wade gunned down my kid brother,...


01:12:08.295 --> 01:12:10.324
...in front of me, 6 years ago in Abeline


01:12:11.007 --> 01:12:12.982
Your brother was a lying (?) card shark


01:12:16.576 --> 01:12:22.205
That is, if he is the asshole I remember, he could of course
be some other asshole I've killed that I've forgot about


01:12:36.468 --> 01:12:38.738
You can't do that... that's immoral.


01:12:41.213 --> 01:12:42.871
Immoral ain't got a damned thing to do with it


01:12:47.921 --> 01:12:50.604
I was expecting to collect a $200 reward for that man.


01:12:53.040 --> 01:12:56.302
I'm delivering him to Contention, I need that money.


01:12:57.136 --> 01:12:59.664
Need it bad enough to die?


01:13:08.626 --> 01:13:11.513
At least let us take our horses.


01:13:12.338 --> 01:13:13.782
I've got no problem with that


01:13:14.482 --> 01:13:16.172
As long as you ride away, Mr.


01:13:17.714 --> 01:13:19.958
Nice knowing you, Dan


01:14:37.270 --> 01:14:38.197
God damn it!


01:14:52.535 --> 01:14:56.679
Did we make it? Did we get away?


01:14:56.886 --> 01:14:59.537
Yeah, Doc. We did


01:15:01.463 --> 01:15:02.804
Thanks to you.


01:15:26.232 --> 01:15:31.021
We need a place to lay low, keep him
out of sight 'till the train comes


01:15:32.119 --> 01:15:36.015
There is a hotel up here, I'll check to see, and you ride around back


01:15:45.816 --> 01:15:49.859
Hey, Will. You keep a watch on the
rail head You see them coming...


01:15:49.944 --> 01:15:51.289
I'll let you know


01:15:52.536 --> 01:15:53.518
William!


01:16:11.249 --> 01:16:13.249
There's a Can-Can on the outs, if you're interested...


01:16:30.747 --> 01:16:33.943
It's the Bridal Suite, I hope you don't mind, it's all they had


01:16:50.256 --> 01:16:53.361
Well, well. That looks like rain clouds over Bigsby


01:16:54.423 --> 01:16:56.830
You still need that $200, Dan?


01:16:56.843 --> 01:16:58.152
Shut up


01:17:00.300 --> 01:17:03.617
Mr.. Evans, you continue to give me great confidence


01:17:06.700 --> 01:17:09.042
I'm going to see about the Marshal.


01:17:25.826 --> 01:17:31.227
We're looking for a group escorting
and outlaw by the name of Ben Wade


01:17:31.586 --> 01:17:33.593
Yeah, we've been chasing them through these tunnels


01:17:39.541 --> 01:17:40.435
Who you are?


01:17:41.013 --> 01:17:42.028
What's it to you?


01:17:43.189 --> 01:17:44.848
Ben Wade killed my brother.


01:17:45.590 --> 01:17:47.598
Then your brother must be famous


01:17:51.318 --> 01:17:54.963
Are you, boys, some kind of posse?


01:18:05.782 --> 01:18:07.408
I hate posse's


01:18:15.479 --> 01:18:17.006
So this is the Bridal Suite.


01:18:18.359 --> 01:18:22.134
Now, I wonder how many brides have taken in this view


01:18:25.975 --> 01:18:27.666
What are you going to do with your $200.00 now, Dan?


01:18:28.151 --> 01:18:29.678
Now that the rains are coming


01:18:31.161 --> 01:18:34.390
I owe people money Wade, that drought left me in the hole


01:18:37.656 --> 01:18:39.478
What do you think about double that amount?


01:18:41.113 --> 01:18:44.593
You can pay your debts, buy a hundred more cows


01:18:45.561 --> 01:18:46.706
Build a new barn


01:18:47.225 --> 01:18:48.654
How do you reckon I'm going to do that?


01:18:51.352 --> 01:18:54.615
Just lay down your gun and let me walk out the door.
It's worth $400.00 (?)


01:18:56.826 --> 01:18:58.320
Is that what you reckon my price is?


01:18:59.673 --> 01:19:00.720
No...


01:19:03.129 --> 01:19:07.293
No, I reckon it's a thousand, One thousand dollars


01:19:07.450 --> 01:19:09.938
There was ten times that amount in Butterfield's coach


01:19:11.001 --> 01:19:13.871
Do you want my cut, Dan? It's all yours.


01:19:15.227 --> 01:19:17.431
Isn't that kind of reckless of you Wade?


01:19:18.474 --> 01:19:21.874
Seeing that... Hmmm. You're so sure
that your crew is coming to get you


01:19:23.802 --> 01:19:24.915
Oh, they're coming, Dan


01:19:26.778 --> 01:19:28.851
Sure as God's vengeance, they're coming


01:19:31.930 --> 01:19:33.686
But I just like to do things easy


01:19:36.154 --> 01:19:38.162
Imagine what you can do with $1000,00 Dan?


01:19:39.324 --> 01:19:42.390
You can hire a couple of ranch hands. Your
boys could go to school, grow up smart.


01:19:43.355 --> 01:19:44.916
What about Alice?


01:19:46.075 --> 01:19:49.239
She wouuld be the proud wife of a bonafide Arizona rancher


01:19:52.316 --> 01:19:54.039
All you've got to do is say yes


01:20:02.492 --> 01:20:07.413
Will you give me a bank note, Wade? Or will
you be kind enough to make a deposit for me?


01:20:07.996 --> 01:20:08.945
Cash.


01:20:13.948 --> 01:20:18.803
You tell me, Wade. How will I account for that amount of money?


01:20:20.828 --> 01:20:23.928
What will I tell people when I spend it?


01:20:24.285 --> 01:20:30.036
That you got the jump on me, you escaped,
and somehow I got a fortune


01:20:34.013 --> 01:20:35.355
No. How dumb do you think people are?


01:20:36.478 --> 01:20:37.722
Nobody needs to know


01:20:41.886 --> 01:20:42.834
Do you know what?


01:20:43.422 --> 01:20:44.218
Would you do me a favor?


01:20:45.823 --> 01:20:47.349
Don't talk to me for a while.


01:20:48.542 --> 01:20:50.269
You mean we're still not friends?


01:20:51.006 --> 01:20:55.032
No. No, we're not


01:20:56.766 --> 01:21:00.989
Come 5 minutes to 3, we're going to be
a hell of a lot closer than you think


01:21:42.017 --> 01:21:42.583
Who is it?


01:21:43.073 --> 01:21:44.221
It's me, Dan


01:21:44.993 --> 01:21:45.941
I brought help


01:21:46.913 --> 01:21:49.738
You've been gone for a long time, Mr. Butterfield


01:21:50.081 --> 01:21:53.383
How do I know someone ain't got a gun on you out there?


01:22:07.938 --> 01:22:10.043
Dan, this is Marshal Will Doane


01:22:10.914 --> 01:22:13.216
Marshal
- Mr. Evans


01:22:15.266 --> 01:22:17.175
Two of my finest men


01:22:23.202 --> 01:22:25.922
I'm sorry about all that Marshal, I am grateful for the help


01:22:26.210 --> 01:22:27.225
Don't mention it


01:22:27.714 --> 01:22:30.470
So, you fellows are really going to help to put me on this train?


01:22:31.458 --> 01:22:33.465
It might not seem like it, Mr.. Wade,


01:22:34.371 --> 01:22:36.672
But we got law and order in this town, just like in any other


01:22:36.963 --> 01:22:39.768
Well, that's very reassuring, Marshal


01:22:40.163 --> 01:22:41.887
How much money is Butterfield paying you?


01:22:42.435 --> 01:22:44.580
That's not of your business


01:22:45.219 --> 01:22:46.081
You're coming with us?


01:22:46.755 --> 01:22:47.933
I'll be walking with you


01:22:49.091 --> 01:22:50.335
Every step of the way.


01:22:52.035 --> 01:22:53.083
You have my word on that, Dan


01:22:53.859 --> 01:22:57.162
That makes five of us, five is good


01:23:00.618 --> 01:23:02.081
It ain't enough


01:23:02.116 --> 01:23:03.545
It ain't nearly enough


01:23:26.245 --> 01:23:27.074
Pa!


01:23:27.461 --> 01:23:28.323
That's my boy


01:23:31.045 --> 01:23:31.809
They're coming.


01:23:34.437 --> 01:23:35.785
They are coming this way, I've seen them
- Where?


01:23:35.877 --> 01:23:37.884
About a mile out, same way we come


01:23:38.245 --> 01:23:39.968
How many are they?
- Seven,... Eight.


01:23:40.357 --> 01:23:42.699
Which is it? 7 or 8?


01:23:45.370 --> 01:23:46.515
Seven.


01:23:57.275 --> 01:24:01.781
Folks, sorry to bother you, but I'm going to
need you to move outside as quickly as possible


01:24:02.650 --> 01:24:06.196
That's it, folks. Move along


01:24:15.631 --> 01:24:16.427
Right there.


01:24:34.480 --> 01:24:38.441
Sure there're a lot of them
- You'd figure, with it being the whole gang


01:25:03.185 --> 01:25:05.192
Boss? Boss?


01:25:07.985 --> 01:25:08.933
Boss, are you are in there?


01:25:10.322 --> 01:25:11.631
What do you want me to tell them?


01:25:13.458 --> 01:25:15.760
You tell them you'll write them a letter every day from Yuma


01:25:24.498 --> 01:25:25.643
Be careful, Wade.


01:25:30.930 --> 01:25:32.841
Charlie, Boys.


01:25:35.059 --> 01:25:38.026
Charlie, why don't you take the boys
down to the saloon and buy them a drink


01:25:40.147 --> 01:25:41.293
Are you ok?


01:25:42.451 --> 01:25:45.353
I am fine. Just sitting up here with my 4 new friends


01:25:48.051 --> 01:25:49.163
That's enough


01:25:54.164 --> 01:25:55.309
Thank You, Charlie.


01:26:15.572 --> 01:26:16.466
Listen up!


01:26:17.141 --> 01:26:18.253
Listen up!


01:26:20.181 --> 01:26:22.003
That's Ben Wade they have up there!


01:26:23.445 --> 01:26:25.550
Ben Wade!


01:26:30.293 --> 01:26:33.838
Now, the railroad intends...


01:26:36.629 --> 01:26:41.169
...to put him on the 3:10 to Yuma and hang him


01:26:42.230 --> 01:26:43.343
What's he doing?


01:26:49.525 --> 01:26:53.355
We will give you $300 cash


01:26:54.677 --> 01:26:57.973
To any man who shoots anyone of his captors


01:26:59.382 --> 01:27:02.928
$200 cash guaranteed!


01:27:09.078 --> 01:27:11.861
$200 guaranteed!


01:27:17.815 --> 01:27:18.960
I'll take $200 Give me the money


01:27:19.286 --> 01:27:21.010
You've got to shoot them first


01:27:27.448 --> 01:27:29.750
It's gotta be 30 or 40 with guns out there now


01:27:31.512 --> 01:27:32.560
The hell with this!


01:27:33.970 --> 01:27:35.970
Now, just a minute Marshall


01:27:37.099 --> 01:27:43.299
Now, look. If it's a fair fight, sure.
I'd stay for that. A fair fight...


01:27:43.870 --> 01:27:45.871
That's a man's duty, but...


01:27:46.754 --> 01:27:48.754
There's only 5 of us


01:27:49.489 --> 01:27:53.172
I'm sorry, Mr, but I'm not going to die here today


01:27:56.731 --> 01:27:58.031
And neither are my men


01:27:58.042 --> 01:27:59.042
Marshall,...


01:28:02.195 --> 01:28:04.495
You forgot this


01:28:08.902 --> 01:28:09.763
Marshall?


01:28:16.022 --> 01:28:19.582
Now, you see Dan, Generally,...


01:28:19.654 --> 01:28:20.799
...pretty much everyone...


01:28:21.478 --> 01:28:22.405
...wants to live


01:28:22.757 --> 01:28:24.006
I'll double your money


01:28:24.198 --> 01:28:25.180
Let's go, boys


01:28:25.734 --> 01:28:28.320
Please, do you want to see us shot down in the street?


01:28:28.710 --> 01:28:29.856
This thing happened in Bigsby


01:28:30.438 --> 01:28:31.518
That means Butterfield too


01:28:31.879 --> 01:28:33.224
Why bring your troubles to Contention?


01:28:33.415 --> 01:28:36.103
We've got families, everyone of us is a family man


01:28:36.391 --> 01:28:37.536
I'm a family man too


01:28:38.503 --> 01:28:40.845
He's gonna walk out on you


01:28:41.767 --> 01:28:44.676
Then you'd best get out like the rest of us


01:28:48.422 --> 01:28:52.318
He isn't gonna come back up here
He's gonna walk out on you


01:28:52.904 --> 01:28:58.410
Now, what you've got to figure is
why you and your boy are gonna die...


01:29:01.352 --> 01:29:04.457
...because of Butterfield's railroad loss of money?


01:29:32.777 --> 01:29:33.922
They're all of them?


01:29:39.018 --> 01:29:39.911
Almost.


01:29:42.762 --> 01:29:44.006
Your move, general


01:29:48.138 --> 01:29:49.898
What do you expect him to say?


01:29:50.314 --> 01:29:51.874
I expect him to say something, that makes sense.


01:29:52.842 --> 01:29:54.987
Something that might save the two of you.


01:29:55.449 --> 01:29:59.076
Take a look Dan, what's the matter?
You don't want to see?


01:30:00.043 --> 01:30:01.025
I'll see them soon enough


01:30:01.994 --> 01:30:03.222
What about you, kid?
You wanna look?


01:30:03.243 --> 01:30:04.453
Stay away from the window, William.


01:30:04.971 --> 01:30:06.181
Go on take a look.


01:30:07.914 --> 01:30:10.638
They're animals, all of them


01:30:15.147 --> 01:30:17.772
They're gonna kill you and your father, William


01:30:19.947 --> 01:30:22.102
And I'll laugh while they do it


01:30:22.411 --> 01:30:23.589
I think you know that


01:30:24.204 --> 01:30:25.316
Call them them off


01:30:27.680 --> 01:30:28.628
Why should I?


01:30:29.375 --> 01:30:30.520
Because you're not all bad


01:30:35.328 --> 01:30:36.473
Yes, I am


01:30:37.344 --> 01:30:39.733
Your saved us from those Indians.
- I saved myself


01:30:40.543 --> 01:30:43.019
You got us through the tunnels, you helped us get away


01:30:43.393 --> 01:30:47.135
If I had a gun in them tunnels, I would've used it on you.


01:30:51.681 --> 01:30:52.608
I don't believe you.


01:30:53.121 --> 01:30:57.911
Kid, I wouldn't last 5 minutes leading an outfit like that
if I wasn't rotten as hell.


01:31:17.793 --> 01:31:18.742
Dan,...


01:31:27.779 --> 01:31:28.727
I can't do it,


01:31:29.123 --> 01:31:31.806
Dan, and if I can't do it, you shouldn't do it either


01:31:34.691 --> 01:31:36.513
They say discretion is the better part of valor


01:31:36.898 --> 01:31:38.855
If you think that you have an
olbigation to me or to the railroad...


01:31:39.106 --> 01:31:42.554
...I assure you! You do not, I'm releasing you


01:31:43.043 --> 01:31:46.491
It's just you left Dan, just you and your boy


01:31:47.075 --> 01:31:50.280
Maybe he is right Pa, maybe we should go home


01:31:57.444 --> 01:32:00.444
What did Doc Potter gave his life for, William?


01:32:01.660 --> 01:32:02.660
And McElroy?


01:32:02.758 --> 01:32:04.417
Little red ants on a hill


01:32:04.452 --> 01:32:08.713
I'll pay you the $200,00 Dan, Right now.
And you can walk away


01:32:13.253 --> 01:32:16.995
You know, this whole ride, it's been nagging on me...


01:32:19.492 --> 01:32:21.859
...that's what the government gave me for my leg...


01:32:23.493 --> 01:32:26.810
...$198.36 and the funny thing is that...


01:32:27.412 --> 01:32:30.661
...when you think about it...
... -which I've been lately-


01:32:30.748 --> 01:32:38.235
Is that they weren't paying me to walk away.
They were paying me, so they could walk away.


01:32:40.134 --> 01:32:42.109
Don't muddy the past on the present, Dan


01:32:42.342 --> 01:32:45.447
No, no, no, Wade, I'm seeing the world the way it is


01:32:46.277 --> 01:32:49.047
If you take him to the train Pa', I'm going with you


01:32:49.126 --> 01:32:51.747
No, Mr. Butterfield's gonna take you home


01:32:52.198 --> 01:32:54.305
No, I'm not going any...
- Yes, you are


01:32:54.438 --> 01:32:55.750
I'm staying here with you


01:32:56.039 --> 01:32:59.800
You're going to hold up in the room across
the hall. You're going to wait until we leave.


01:33:00.295 --> 01:33:02.684
I'll get him to Bigsby, you've got my promise


01:33:02.950 --> 01:33:04.579
You're going to promise a lot more than that, Butterfield


01:33:05.639 --> 01:33:13.058
I want guarantees that Hollander and his
boys will never set foot on my land again


01:33:13.446 --> 01:33:20.750
And that my water is going to flow, and I expect you to hand
my wife $1000.00 cash when you see her, you've got money to spare


01:33:20.935 --> 01:33:24.797
I can deliver that, just get him on the train.


01:33:26.631 --> 01:33:28.933
You heard him?
- I heard him.


01:33:31.047 --> 01:33:32.389
William...


01:33:33.224 --> 01:33:35.525
...I want you to give this back to your mother


01:33:37.640 --> 01:33:43.430
I want you to tell her, it helped me find what is right


01:33:48.585 --> 01:33:52.927
Pa, I can't just leave you


01:33:53.289 --> 01:33:58.984
I'm going to be a day behind you William, unless something
happens, and if it does, I need a man at the ranch


01:33:59.944 --> 01:34:04.517
To run things, to protect our family, and I know that you can do that, because you've become a fine man William.


01:34:05.801 --> 01:34:07.940
You've become a fine man, you've got all the best parts of me...


01:34:09.258 --> 01:34:10.403
...what few there are


01:34:15.593 --> 01:34:24.078
And you just remember that your old man hauled
Ben Wade to that station when nobody else would


01:35:16.556 --> 01:35:19.442
You know, squeezing that watch won't stop time


01:35:26.380 --> 01:35:27.689
Don't get so scared.


01:35:28.108 --> 01:35:29.253
You might (pack?) a bad mood.


01:35:37.390 --> 01:35:38.819
Ever read the Bible, Dan?


01:35:41.422 --> 01:35:51.281
I read it one time, I was 8 years old, my daddy had just got himself killed over a shot of whiskey, and my mom said we were going back East to start over


01:35:52.750 --> 01:35:57.093
So she gave me a Bible, sat me down at the train station. Told me to read it


01:36:00.431 --> 01:36:01.958
She was going to get our tickets


01:36:04.430 --> 01:36:09.481
Well, I did what she said...
I read that Bible cover to cover.


01:36:09.806 --> 01:36:10.951
It took me 3 days


01:36:14.382 --> 01:36:15.527
She never came back.


01:36:41.168 --> 01:36:42.029
It's time


01:36:58.832 --> 01:37:00.972
It's a half mile to the station from here, Dan


01:37:04.817 --> 01:37:05.864
I guess we're walking


01:37:43.602 --> 01:37:44.552
Lucky


01:37:48.147 --> 01:37:48.779
Dan...


01:38:20.788 --> 01:38:23.992
You're not gonna get a chance to use those Scofields, Charlie


01:38:25.301 --> 01:38:28.985
Perhaps you can explain to me the next portion of your plan, Dan


01:38:51.446 --> 01:38:53.333
Hey! Hey!


01:38:54.006 --> 01:38:57.235
Not the black hat!


01:38:57.974 --> 01:39:01.079
(?) you dumb shits!


01:39:11.350 --> 01:39:12.179
Charlie.


01:39:15.767 --> 01:39:17.076
Get back! Get back!


01:39:22.967 --> 01:39:23.828
Boss!


01:39:28.695 --> 01:39:31.695
Let's go! White Door! Move it!


01:39:54.264 --> 01:39:55.442
I can't do this no more, Dan


01:40:00.985 --> 01:40:02.130
I'm putting you on that train, Wade


01:40:02.165 --> 01:40:06.935
I'm going back! Your boy is gone hero.
Ain't nobody watching no more


01:40:07.609 --> 01:40:11.424
You still got that one good leg,
why don't you use it to get on home?


01:40:12.121 --> 01:40:12.982
Charlie!


01:40:14.617 --> 01:40:15.380
Charlie Prince!


01:40:15.769 --> 01:40:17.776
Yeah, boss!
- Hold your fire!


01:40:18.265 --> 01:40:19.159
I'm walking out


01:40:44.091 --> 01:40:46.780
I have never been no hero, Wade


01:40:48.891 --> 01:40:51.608
Only action I've seen, it was a retreat...


01:40:52.475 --> 01:40:54.777
...my foot got shot off by one of my own men.


01:40:56.699 --> 01:40:59.601
You try telling that story to your boy...


01:41:00.379 --> 01:41:01.873
...see how he looks at you then


01:41:17.244 --> 01:41:18.106
Boss!


01:41:22.748 --> 01:41:23.861
Ok, Dan


01:41:34.653 --> 01:41:35.580
Son.


01:41:37.691 --> 01:41:40.676
They're on the move, they're on the move!


01:41:41.816 --> 01:41:44.885
Boss, Boss..


01:42:18.393 --> 01:42:19.393
Can you make this?
- Yeah


01:43:21.927 --> 01:43:22.714
Spread out!...


01:43:34.824 --> 01:43:36.783
What time is it?


01:43:37.223 --> 01:43:38.190
Quarter past three


01:43:38.758 --> 01:43:40.961
Where is the 3:10 to Yuma?


01:43:41.062 --> 01:43:42.021
Running late, I suppose


01:43:42.837 --> 01:43:43.937
How late?


01:43:45.113 --> 01:43:45.913
Beats me


01:43:45.954 --> 01:43:47.009
It gets here when it gets here


01:43:48.355 --> 01:43:50.561
God damned trains, You never can rely on them, huh?


01:44:28.748 --> 01:44:33.880
You know... I ain't stubborn.


01:44:34.681 --> 01:44:35.640
Excuse me?


01:44:36.888 --> 01:44:41.116
You said I was stubborn for keeping my family on a dying ranch


01:44:43.457 --> 01:44:44.757
It's my son, Mark


01:44:45.329 --> 01:44:46.430
The young one


01:44:47.149 --> 01:44:49.849
He got tuberculosis when he was 2


01:44:51.424 --> 01:44:54.424
Doctor said he'd die if he didn't have a dry climate


01:44:54.920 --> 01:44:56.454
Why are you telling me this?


01:44:58.661 --> 01:44:59.620
I don't know


01:45:00.676 --> 01:45:04.608
I guess that I just wanted you to know that...


01:45:04.897 --> 01:45:08.734
...I ain't stubborn. That's all


01:45:41.511 --> 01:45:44.511
Well, as long as we're making confesions
- Yeah?


01:45:45.179 --> 01:45:49.303
I've been to Yuma Prison before


01:45:49.400 --> 01:45:52.565
Twice Escaped twice too


01:46:55.578 --> 01:46:58.934
First car, sliding door


01:47:09.624 --> 01:47:10.724
They'll be coming


01:47:49.384 --> 01:47:52.467
I've got a prisoner to go to Yuma


01:47:57.824 --> 01:47:59.948
Well, you did it, Dan


01:48:01.570 --> 01:48:02.170
No!


01:48:12.116 --> 01:48:14.322
Pa!


01:48:40.818 --> 01:48:44.846
For a one legged rancher,...


01:48:46.873 --> 01:48:49.846
...he's one tough son of a bitch


01:49:53.976 --> 01:49:54.776
You done it, Pa


01:49:57.943 --> 01:50:02.738
You done it. You got him on the train


01:50:56.543 --> 01:50:57.694
Pa


01:51:58.950 --> 01:51:59.750
[whistles]

